# Habeas Protocol — environment variables
# Copy to `.env` and adjust for your local setup. The API and the property
# tests both read from the live shell environment, not from this file
# directly — source it via `set -a; . ./.env; set +a` or use direnv.

# --- Postgres (the local research DB) ----------------------------------
# `scripts/postgres_local.sh` provisions a local Postgres at the path
# below; values match its defaults.
PGHOST=localhost
PGPORT=5433
PGUSER=hamza
PGDATABASE=habeas

# --- API server bind ---------------------------------------------------
# Loopback-only by default. Do NOT bind to 0.0.0.0 without first reading
# api/server.py: there is no auth and CORS is scoped to localhost.
HABEAS_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
HABEAS_API_PORT=5544

# --- API write-mode gate ----------------------------------------------
# Set to "1" to enable POST /api/rule_save (rule authoring back to disk).
# Off by default; the dashboard authoring tab will surface a clear error
# until this is enabled.
# HABEAS_ADMIN_MODE=1

# --- Property-test trial multiplier -----------------------------------
# Bumps every property's trial count. Default 50 (yields 1930 invariants
# total at the time of writing). CI sets this to 100 for stricter checks.
# HABEAS_PROPERTY_TRIALS=50

# --- Catala toolchain --------------------------------------------------
# The Catala compiler is expected on PATH after `eval $(opam env --switch=catala)`.
# If it is at a non-standard location, override:
# HABEAS_CATALA=/full/path/to/catala
